{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now","id":1525755,"title":"What do want to see from VTM now?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-11-21T15:29:12-08:00","id":1525755,"title":"What do want to see from VTM now?","content":"I would like to see some variation of The Children Of Night sourcebook with newer characters and updates on preexisting characters with new plot ideas to go with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T02:31:12-08:00","id":1525777,"title":"","content":"Well, what I'd want is for Bloodlines 2 to come out, it not be nearly the hot commodity Paradox is banking on, and them finally giving up on the vain dream that they have the ability to resurrect VtM as a major brand without actually putting the work to rebuild that brand. Paradox needs to recognize that they are not a TTRPG company, they've gone through multiple core partners and have PR problem after PR problem after PR problem; at a certain point it can't be the companies licensing from Paradox that's the problem (even if the part of the problem is that Paradox sucks at picking people to make their stuff, which seems pretty true on the video-game side of the brand).<br /> <br /> While part of me wants Paradox to sell the IPs to someone else, there's very few companies that are actually going to be better that can afford something like that. Paradox needs to find someone to manage the brand that's actually going to recognize the brand is limping at best on the excitement of V5's release having some decent hype. They need someone that understands what Paradox wants out of new TTRPG books (existing brand recognition to expand into far more profitable products), and then give that person the authority and financial backing to start a new era. Whether it's V5 or V6 or whatever. They need better community engagement, more outreach to communities that the past teams have just tossed under the bus, and also the spine to do things like cancel licenses if a partner is actually dragging them down (By Night Studio's bullshit this weekend) rather than just making something that isn't the personal vision of someone at Paradox (dumping Hunter Studio's version of W5 that seems like it would have been much better received by the fans but wasn't to the individual tastes of one person at Paradox who isn't the audience for the entire game). They need to stop giving a shit about when on the calendar GenCon is so they stop rushing major releases and causing themselves far more problems that whatever perceived benefit of having a GenCon release date is.<br /> <br /> After that? I'd want an edition of VtM that fulfills for more people what V5 promised to be: a version of VtM for the 21st century. They had so much talent available to them, and it was squandered on ideas that weren't fresh in 2010. If they want a system that's better suited for translation to a video game? Fine, actually commit to that. If they want a true rules-light that can expand to taste take on VtM? Commit to that. Professional skilled game designers can make fun games with those sorts of directives in mind; but games suffer if direction gets yanked around a lot.<br /> <br /> Then give us board games, card games app versions of those games, novels, comics, whatever else. Build the brand up with actual stuff people will enjoy. Let gamers know VtM is back for real, and in the background Paradox is doing two things for their own good: funding marketing and distribution that smaller companies can't do on their own to hit large audiences (esp. other languages), and use the laid out well defined vision for what VtM is supposed to be to work on video games in the background so that once gamers feel like VtM is really back, then you can show to an even wider audience something big, and real, and actually plant a flag for VtM that it still has it's own space in mainstream pop culture.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T03:27:42-08:00","id":1525779,"title":"","content":"V6<br /> Elders<br /> Expanded game play (no street level limitations, Masquerade is about global conspirancy, mithology and horror, give this)<br /> Only Generation (no Blood Potency)<br /> New meta plot, whitout &quot;dead ends&quot; like MCU <br /> Traits level 6+ (return of god like elder vampires, true antagonists of the game)<br /> Return of unique disciplines (no excuse for lame writers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T05:58:20-08:00","id":1525787,"title":"","content":"Elders<br /> sabbat play<br /> Path play<br /> Expanded support for alt play style<br /> Loose the no unique discipline mandate.<br /> Less railroading<br /> stop writting fluff for soft retcons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-22-2023, 10:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T07:58:30-08:00","id":1525794,"title":"","content":"As with other posters, most of what I want is the same thing.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Bloodlines 2</b></u> <br /> Just let it be good, the original was lightning in a bottle as far as storyline, writing, and atmosphere so I don't expect the sequel to be its equivalent, but I would like it to be at least as good as VtM Redemption.<br /> <br /> <u><b>V6</b></u> <br /> The hard left turn that V5 made as far as story scale, metaplot, and sad to say progressive politics always felt like a cash grab to reach a theoretical wider audience. I feel that V6 should be more neutral. Rather than a metaplot driven game line, the WoD catalogue should be more plug and play with its design and modules. Basically all factions and systems are optional. The game line &quot;All Flesh Must Be Eaten&quot; comes to mind, with how each supplement gives optional and expansion rules, rather than rules and backstory bloat. As others have said, make sure V6 actually supports other styles of play beyond street level, yes the lost boys are cool, but so is vampire Amazon or vampire Microsoft. The rules need to be a bit more robust for elder play and established vampires who are doing societal chess moves.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Virtual Tabletop app</b></u> <br /> As much as TTRPGs and LARP are the historical core of VtM gaming, the reality is that the current state of the world is just not conducive to in person play. So a somewhat robust VTTP app is a part of the answer. The app should integrate ST tools, a PDF library, and group VOIP functions. Preferably with tools that allow for maps to be displayed and character portraits to be easily uploaded and highlighted when the person is speaking.<br /> <br /> As for the monetization of the app, I would suggest that the app itself is free, with the basic character sheet functionality, dice roller program, and ST functions being available. The monetization comes from the notion that you can purchase a full price physical copy and scan the QR code for a free digital copy to unlock in the app, or you pay half price to just unlock the PDF in the app and forgo the physical copy. This is based on the concept in UK law that says you are allowed to keep a digital copy of any physical media you own. Then once this is formalized and stabilized, create a similar app for each game line. Perhaps this VtM app would be where the more simulation-esque aspects of the game could be run and tracked.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Vampire City Builder</u></b> <br /> Yes this is an out of left field idea, but it should be within the realms of possibility. Think of a game such as Frostpunk where your focus is a single city with an overworld map to interact with. You are the Prince/Baron/etc. of the city and you have to contend with various factions, influence how the city itself develops, what vampire laws you choose to enforce or ignore, plan for invasions by other supernaturals or mortal hunters. Ironically the notion of having a vampire leader solves the immersion breaking aspect of many city builders where the same leader runs things from the stone age to the far future. This can then be expanded upon by having different scenarios such as a city in the dark ages, or in the post apocalypse. Alternatively, you get replayability from the concept that as Prince you can choose what your supernatural population consists of. Running a city of only Nagaraja will have very different design than say an all Toreador city. But a city with a mix of clans, bloodlines, and other supernaturals will play out differently based on what critters are in the mix. It is crucial that the developer understand the grim dark nature of WoD, perhaps get the maker of Frostpunk and This War of Mine to make the game, since they seem to have a better grasp on dark morality than many western developers.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Netflix Series</u></b> <br /> Just pull the trigger on making a small-scale series to raise awareness of the WoD. I would suggest an animated series so that special effects are not a limiting factor for the series. Spend the money on good voice actors and non-woke writers who enjoy the setting and the source material and want to make a love letter to it, rather than using the setting to spread their politics or ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T09:18:01-08:00","id":1525796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525794#post1525794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><u>Netflix Series</u></b><br /> Just pull the trigger on making a small-scale series to raise awareness of the WoD. I would suggest an animated series so that special effects are not a limiting factor for the series. Spend the money on good voice actors and non-woke writers who enjoy the setting and the source material and want to make a love letter to it, rather than using the setting to spread their politics or ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also wanted to and I think they have or had plans for something like that, but based on the fifth editions, this partly explains some changes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T11:30:33-08:00","id":1525803,"title":"","content":"Well, a V6 that don't inflict Humanity tenants as behavioral basis would be sweet. Also, unique disciplines were sweet, improve the clan weaknesses (technology? Really? So Lasombras were virtually perfect until circa 1995? How aren't they the biggest ludites ever?) Take Lasombras and Nagajara from the Family Reunion, for Chrissake, they have no connection whatsoever with Cappadocius. Drop blood potency, it works wonderfully on Requiem, but not on Masquerade. Elders, elders, elders, they're part of the oppressive climate of VtM. Work better on the hunger mechanics, it has merits but great concept, bad execution. Highly human and no human vampires should come back. Golconda and dark paths should be available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T11:39:33-08:00","id":1525806,"title":"","content":"A netflix or anime series on VTM would be interesting to see and I hope that they would stay true to the lore of the game. But I tend to be wary when they try to make movies based off such games as it always been more misses then hits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T11:41:39-08:00","id":1525807,"title":"","content":"I am a simple soul<br /> Leave the whole V5 &quot;failed experiment&quot; behind (okay, I know for some unfathomable reason there are people who like V5, tastes differ I get it, treat it like Requiem, or an alternate universe WoD; someone botched their Temporis and made a timeline with... that), and continue from Becketts Jyhad Diary and the V20 line with a V30<br /> Give back the whole enchilada to Onyx Path Publishing - they knew what they were doing, heck even in V5 their supplements were superb!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T13:12:27-08:00","id":1525808,"title":"","content":"<br /> I was very fond of the original pitch of the Anarchs being &quot;the place where most vampires just end up as discarded tools&quot;, and I'd be very interested in a City-book detailing an Anarch-run place.<br /> <br /> A book on the Circolatory System and Blood, on expanding the role of feeding and of victims in chronicles,could be very frightening but also important in setting the tone of the edition.<br /> <br /> A book on the Nosferatu underbelly, the Goblin Roads, Night Couriers, Nomad Packs, Ravnos wanderers and all other outcasts going around in strange, dangerous and fringe places.<br /> <br /> I'd be happy if &quot;Blood Stained Love&quot; paved the way for some sourcebooks providing ideas and tools to create different kind of horror chronicles and themes.<br /> <br /> A book about the Gehenna War, with informations on the Ashirra and some advice on how to run Elders in the V5 framework, would be useful too.<br /> <br /> A sourcebook about Asia, detailing the not-Kue Jin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In the world of &quot;I'd like but difficult to see&quot;, a Children of the Night supplement would be interesting for us nostalgics. Generally speaking, a bit more metaplot would of course be useful and nice. Also, following on the Fall of London theme, some chronicle books detailing other relevant Falls (Fall of Berlin, Fall of Venice, Fall of Prague, Fall of Wien, Fall of Mexico City) and something on the new Infernal Trinity in Istanbul.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> On the subject of who's steering the ship, I'm fairly positive on the latest books but not keen on the soft-retcons on the original books: I'd be divided about bringing the license back to OPP, as they did really solid work on their supplements, but I feel that in an effort to bridge divides they soft-retconned a bit too much of the original pitch of V5, particularly on the role of the Camarilla. But I really love their philological yet open ended approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> In case of V6, I'd keep most of the V5 framework, especially Hunger and streamlined combat. PLEASE PLEASE PLEASE don't bring back unique disciplines, levels over 6, Paths of Thaumaturgy. And also PLEASE PLEASE PLEASE go on with this global approach with presenting things: I'm really happy that the assumed setting is not 100% modelled on an American metropolis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-22-2023, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T19:16:35-08:00","id":1525818,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12590\" data-vbnamecard=\"12590\">Manfr</a>, might I interest you in Vampire the Requiem? Some of the things you seem to treasure highly in V5 are treated fairly competently in Requiem. The lack of elder powers, by chance. Since very high blood potency make feeding pretty tough, elder vampires go in torpor to weaken the blood, with the side effect of eating the memories, so, elder vampires are not such a threat. And like that they lose access to higher levels of discipline. Also, with the lineages the game is very global in general. If you haven't already, give a chance to Requiem, and you may be very positively impressed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-22T21:13:07-08:00","id":1525821,"title":"","content":"Does only official material count?<br /> <br /> Because in the last few years the authors of the Storytellers Vault have been killing it, especially in the historical setting departement. For me who only plays Vampire or WOD in general in historical settings christmas was coming every 5-6 months or so.<br /> <br /> Just to name some:<br /> <br /> Rome by Night Via Desideratio<br /> <br /> Vampire Age of the Living Gods<br /> <br /> Werewolf The Savage Age<br /> <br /> I am happily settling with everything the wonderful authors of the ST-Vault are creating, while exploring content no official source would ever touch.<br /> <br /> What I would want:<br /> <br /> Just more material for the settings above <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25379-spacedigger","name":"Spacedigger","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T05:18:30-08:00","id":1525834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525818#post1525818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12590\" data-vbnamecard=\"12590\">Manfr</a>, might I interest you in Vampire the Requiem? Some of the things you seem to treasure highly in V5 are treated fairly competently in Requiem. The lack of elder powers, by chance. Since very high blood potency make feeding pretty tough, elder vampires go in torpor to weaken the blood, with the side effect of eating the memories, so, elder vampires are not such a threat. And like that they lose access to higher levels of discipline. Also, with the lineages the game is very global in general. If you haven't already, give a chance to Requiem, and you may be very positively impressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Lord, Vampire The Requiem 2th is the best vampire tabletop game made, my real dream? Take Rosa Bailey and Matthew Dawnkins em give them total criative control to create Vampire The Masquerade 6\u00b0 edition (with base rules of VtR 2th adaptation to Masquerade scenario)<br /> <br /> Forget V5<br /> <br /> This is the perfect world for all fandom of Vampire rpg.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T12:42:53-08:00","id":1525857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525818#post1525818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12590\" data-vbnamecard=\"12590\">Manfr</a>, might I interest you in Vampire the Requiem? Some of the things you seem to treasure highly in V5 are treated fairly competently in Requiem. The lack of elder powers, by chance. Since very high blood potency make feeding pretty tough, elder vampires go in torpor to weaken the blood, with the side effect of eating the memories, so, elder vampires are not such a threat. And like that they lose access to higher levels of discipline. Also, with the lineages the game is very global in general. If you haven't already, give a chance to Requiem, and you may be very positively impressed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In Italy, we just got the corebooks of VtR, WtF, MtA and CtL, as well as a couple of blue books, three Covenant Books, Nomads, Coteries and a couple of Bloodlines books, then the publishing company went out of business and no one bought the license.<br /> <br /> I quite like Requiem! In my association, we were all very fond of VtM but Requiem was bounced hardly: I was able to run just a single campaign when 1st edition came out, but I've followed the line, mostly stopping before 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> That said, I'd be happy to get the chance to translate Requiem material into V5, as there are greater compatibilities between the rulesets: I bet Team Ericsson had a bit of the same idea, using the best bits of VtM and VtR to bring together the fandom, like D&amp;D5e did. \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T12:44:08-08:00","id":1525858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525834#post1525834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good Lord, Vampire The Requiem 2th is the best vampire tabletop game made, my real dream? Take Rosa Bailey and Matthew Dawnkins em give them total criative control to create Vampire The Masquerade 6\u00b0 edition (with base rules of VtR 2th adaptation to Masquerade scenario)<br /> <br /> Forget V5<br /> <br /> This is the perfect world for all fandom of Vampire rpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm the proof it wouldn't be the perfect world, I really like V5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said, the team would be terrific, BUT let me remind you that Matthew was the Lead Creative of V5 for some years <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T12:50:55-08:00","id":1525860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525834#post1525834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good Lord, Vampire The Requiem 2th is the best vampire tabletop game made, my real dream? Take Rosa Bailey and Matthew Dawnkins em give them total criative control to create Vampire The Masquerade 6\u00b0 edition (with base rules of VtR 2th adaptation to Masquerade scenario)<br /> <br /> Forget V5<br /> <br /> This is the perfect world for all fandom of Vampire rpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with importing the logic of <i>Requiem</i> into <i>Masquerade</i> is that <i>Masquerade</i> is not simply a vampire (TT)RPG: it is a cultural artefact that has reached a certain level of aesthetic and thematic stability in the three decades since the release of the game's first edition; to put it simply, <i>Masquerade</i> does not share its &quot;vibe&quot; with <i>Requiem</i> or (to my knowledge) any other vampire RPG on the market. It's just not possible to 'update' <i>Masquerade</i> without confronting and - this is important - working within the established conceits of the setting.<br /> <br /> I'm basically content to resign myself to pre-2015 editions of the game, but: in order for me to invest my resources in any future edition of <i>Masquerade</i>, it must be willing to engage with the world and style of the entire V:tM line beyond the particular tastes of singular players who had the luck to find themselves at the writer's desk; it must seek to expand player options instead of limiting them, in awareness of the different playing styles preferred by separate sections of the community; and do away with excessive nostalgia for the oldest editions of the game at the expense of the rich and diverse setting it has developed since '91.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","user":"gamiem","date":". 11-30-2023, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-23T13:06:13-08:00","id":1525862,"title":"","content":"That's the main thing. Yeah, VtM is a whole social impact. And VtR is great in their own right. But they don't intermingle. V5 is a tragedy because they tried to hammer VtR mechanics in VtM lore, and, really? No, just no. If the Requiem mechanics are to be praised, keep the line going, AS REQUIEM. Because mashing the universes just don't work. The main complaints against V5 (and, frankly, I'll engross the choir) are the VtR things that were willy nilly trounced in VtM. So, again, if Requiem is accepted, publish Requiem, if Masquerade wants to keep going, it must keep going as Masquerade, not this szlatcha of systems. Fans of Requiem are happy, fans of Masquerade are happy, the sales go up. Would be the best solution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-24T17:15:35-08:00","id":1525892,"title":"","content":"I would like a few things, firstly if we were to have more VTM games you could make one based on XCOM where you have to control vampires and face threats in your territory at the same time you have to expand your influence and obtain resources, like getting the market of blood and gather allies to your cause. If there was a story or campaign mode, it could be a group of anarchists facing the Camarilla, but things get complicated, because it always has to happen, and they find themselves in a Camarilla x Sabbat war. Just imagine facing in this context, a chimera made with protean, war ghouls, perhaps even a zombie werewolf, of course a tip to fight hunters too.<br /> <br /> Another option within this context of electronic games would be visual novels, like Cortories of New York, I liked the game at the end of the day, although they could make it a little longer perhaps, and of course give you more control within the story and more ending options, anyone who played knows what I'm talking about, I won't go into details because you know, spoilers. There are a lot of things they can adapt, many by the night, even expand and create some things.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I wouldn't be against a TV series, it might even be unrealistic, but I think that at least with VTM it can be done, we put in a neophyte just to locate those who are not familiar with the original context and we take the opportunity to first introduce the camarilla and its seven founding clans and over time expanding the universe and perhaps even making spin-offs in other environments and circumstances, taking other facets of the WOD.<br /> <br /> Now the elephant in the room, regarding the V5, I'm not totally against it, firstly, I think the SI is a good antagonist or at worst functional, and it has some amalgamation effects that I think are ideas that can be used, however I also think that older vampires work better as final bosses, if you know what I mean, there's also that thing about unique disciplines and 6+, I think it could still be included, but they would need to be moderated, I mean, it's part of the which makes each clan unique and the 6+ disciplines kind of show why an older vampire is stronger, although also having a vampire deal 5 damage to two targets before they can move doesn't work as well mechanically if you stop to To think, then some changes might be welcome and you should be able to use stronger characters if you wanted, although I don't know how it would work in roleplay.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T11:02:04-08:00","id":1525914,"title":"","content":"I like the idea if they gave us a sourcebook on how to create your own by night cities like they did years ago with Damation City with VTR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T12:35:03-08:00","id":1525917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525862#post1525862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the main thing. Yeah, VtM is a whole social impact. And VtR is great in their own right. But they don't intermingle. V5 is a tragedy because they tried to hammer VtR mechanics in VtM lore, and, really? No, just no. If the Requiem mechanics are to be praised, keep the line going, AS REQUIEM. Because mashing the universes just don't work. The main complaints against V5 (and, frankly, I'll engross the choir) are the VtR things that were willy nilly trounced in VtM. So, again, if Requiem is accepted, publish Requiem, if Masquerade wants to keep going, it must keep going as Masquerade, not this szlatcha of systems. Fans of Requiem are happy, fans of Masquerade are happy, the sales go up. Would be the best solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot agree with this logic, honestly: the classic VtM system badly needed a rules overhaul, if it was to be relaunched - otherwise, a 5th edition would have really been just a soulless money grab. V20 already gave us compiled and streamlined &quot;classic&quot; rules, without significant modifications: but between V1 and V5 stood 17 years of evolution of game design.<br /> <br /> The NWOD / COFD lines have developed their own identity in time, but both their rules and their themes are rooted in a re-imagination of the original WOD. To adopt their best practices and ideas, after years of testing, is just sound game design. That was nonetheless supplemented by many other original innovations.<br /> <br /> Bridging this divide with an inter-operable system and a setting which was more flexible and would allow porting of good ideas was a DnD5e-like operation, which I always felt was a good idea: the problem is, they hoped to close edition wars between OWod and CofD, but instead another edition war between Wod5e and Wod20 flared, and I feel this ultimately contributed to killing the CofD. After 19 years and 2 iterations, Chronicles lines had basically published everything a toolbox setting could support, they would have needed a 3rd edition. That however, would have split both the fanbase and marketing budgets way too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-25-2023, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T13:12:38-08:00","id":1525921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525917#post1525917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">otherwise, a 5th edition would have really been just a soulless money grab.</div> </div> </div> </div>It IS just a soulless money grab.<br /> I am willing to die on that hill<br /> You know why the Chicago by Night 5th Edition and its supplements or anything basically Onyx Path Publishing made was a HUGE success?<br /> <i>Kickstarter</i>\u200b<br /> Becasue everything they made was made <i>for the gamers</i>, gave them <i>what they want for their money,</i> not showed everything and the kitchen sink Paradox <i>decided</i> the players want down their throath - or at least tried - and failed misreably<br /> But tried to grab as much cash as inhumanly possible nontheless and still not willing to admit their mistakes and pumping out 5th edition didasters after disasters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T13:20:20-08:00","id":1525923,"title":"","content":"I don't trust the current leadership at Paradox, the current in-house WOD-team or Renegade to really steer this ship to success but if I alone were in charge, what I would wish for would be this:<br /> <br /> For V5:<ul><li>Setting-books. Chicago by Night (and the other affiliated books plus Fall of London) are the only setting-books we've got so far. One of the hallmarks of the Renegade-material has been a very generalist approach to the setting. And whenever things get specific you get fleeting glimpses of worldbuilding that are often awkward, baffling or just straight-up nonsense. It would be nice if a Renegade-supplement actually delved into portraying a specific city/region and trying to do some genuine worldbuilding.</li> <li>Clan-lore. Some have a good amount of lore in V5 but others have barely any lore in V5. Doesn't matter if it contradicts old lore, just actually have lore for how to play Clans and portray them in a game. The current approach isn't giving freedom to players, it's just laziness. The concepts are way too specific to hand them to people at the people with these half-assed presentations. Of course, this means re-treading similar paths to previous editions but V5 wasn't written with a distinct enough vision to not do that. (And both H5 and W5 have suffered in the clumsy and poorly thought-out attempts to divorce those two splats from previous editions.)</li> </ul>Beyond that for WOD5E:<ul><li>It's time to just admit that WOD5E has failed. There was a moment to make WOD5E happen and it was around the time of the release of V5. That moment was squandered due to scandal and it all has gone downhill since then. Especially since the videogame-side was similarly cursed.</li> <li>Instead of re-building some sort of mega-brand with broad appeal, it's time to just meet the fanbase where it is. CofD 3rd edition, WOD 30th Anniversary, WOD6E... all of it will be barely profitable but hey It's something... Clinging to the idea of making WOD5E happen is just a road to nowhere at this point.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T14:22:06-08:00","id":1525929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525917#post1525917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After 19 years and 2 iterations, Chronicles lines had basically published everything a toolbox setting could support, they would have needed a 3rd edition. That however, would have split both the fanbase and marketing budgets way too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>But they published more than toolbox books. In the last years the first edition, we we were getting the books that Knightingale suggested, but for Requiem. Then they sort of gradually fizzle out in the 2010s, years before V5 I\u2019d like to stress.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want new editions, I want developers to stop abandoning the worlds they\u2019ve already started writing. Whether it\u2019s 90s VtM, VTR or V5 can we keep at least one of them going? And screw the toolbox model. If you\u2019d rather homebrew your own setting, go ahead and ignore the new supplements.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T14:24:26-08:00","id":1525931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525917#post1525917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cannot agree with this logic, honestly: the classic VtM system badly needed a rules overhaul, if it was to be relaunched - otherwise, a 5th edition would have really been just a soulless money grab. V20 already gave us compiled and streamlined &quot;classic&quot; rules, without significant modifications: but between V1 and V5 stood 17 years of evolution of game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 is a money grab to predate on nostalgia. Ok, the world changed, the metaphor was diluted, but, still, the WoD public wanted materials to the WoD, not to some kind of Frankenstein of systems. That's why V20 flourished. Lasombra players are not jumping in delight seeing their clan defanged like that. Btw, Lasombras are now Angelis Ater? I really didn't understand why they're necromancers/satanists out of the blue. The fall of Sabbath just dropped a bomb on edgelords, or anyone that wanted to play Vampire as vampires. The current state of the crossover Generation x Blood potency just makes no sense. Touchstones being this imposition over vampires that may not want to have this kind of bond with humanity. Tremeres without thaumaturgy, Lasombras without technology (suddenly the social darwinists are codependent to keep their empires. Great, just great), Diablerie being at least undesirable, Elders not contributing with the pressure (make them make some blood surges and that's all). Frankly? There's a reason WoD and nWoD are two separate materials. They are two different histories, two completely different mythos. If an update is supposed to be made, make un update, not throw the whole thing on the flames and keep the names.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T15:09:45-08:00","id":1525939,"title":"","content":"I want Clanbooks back, they need to stop trying to make Clans obsolete, removing them from the Sabbat and trying the laughable claim that your Predator Type is more influential on a vampire than their Clan. I mean, that may be true if Paradox succeeded in their \u201clol everyone is Anarchs/Thinbloods now, all Elders are dead\u201d plan, but it sure ain\u2019t how fans see the game. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, as an Aussie I\u2019d love to see something dealing with Australia, other than an occasional throwaway line about Prince Sarrasine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T15:28:56-08:00","id":1525940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525834#post1525834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good Lord, Vampire The Requiem 2th is the best vampire tabletop game made, my real dream? Take Rosa Bailey and Matthew Dawnkins em give them total criative control to create Vampire The Masquerade 6\u00b0 edition (with base rules of VtR 2th adaptation to Masquerade scenario)<br /> <br /> Forget V5<br /> <br /> This is the perfect world for all fandom of Vampire rpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would this work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T19:35:39-08:00","id":1525944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525923#post1525923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't trust the current leadership at Paradox, the current in-house WOD-team or Renegade to really steer this ship to success but if I alone were in charge, what I would wish for would be this:<br /> <br /> For V5:<ul><li>Setting-books. Chicago by Night (and the other affiliated books plus Fall of London) are the only setting-books we've got so far. One of the hallmarks of the Renegade-material has been a very generalist approach to the setting. And whenever things get specific you get fleeting glimpses of worldbuilding that are often awkward, baffling or just straight-up nonsense. It would be nice if a Renegade-supplement actually delved into portraying a specific city/region and trying to do some genuine worldbuilding.</li> <li>Clan-lore. Some have a good amount of lore in V5 but others have barely any lore in V5. Doesn't matter if it contradicts old lore, just actually have lore for how to play Clans and portray them in a game. The current approach isn't giving freedom to players, it's just laziness. The concepts are way too specific to hand them to people at the people with these half-assed presentations. Of course, this means re-treading similar paths to previous editions but V5 wasn't written with a distinct enough vision to not do that. (And both H5 and W5 have suffered in the clumsy and poorly thought-out attempts to divorce those two splats from previous editions.)</li> </ul>Beyond that for WOD5E:<ul><li>It's time to just admit that WOD5E has failed. There was a moment to make WOD5E happen and it was around the time of the release of V5. That moment was squandered due to scandal and it all has gone downhill since then. Especially since the videogame-side was similarly cursed.</li> <li>Instead of re-building some sort of mega-brand with broad appeal, it's time to just meet the fanbase where it is. CofD 3rd edition, WOD 30th Anniversary, WOD6E... all of it will be barely profitable but hey It's something... Clinging to the idea of making WOD5E happen is just a road to nowhere at this point.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure WoD5e can\u2019t be salvaged?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-25T21:55:50-08:00","id":1525952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525944#post1525944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure WoD5e can\u2019t be salvaged?</div> </div> </div> </div>H5 and W5 are not exactly glowing endorsements toward it, what with the stripping out of anything that made either of them what they were and the copying of the worst parts of Danganronpa for W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T04:52:29-08:00","id":1525956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525944#post1525944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you sure WoD5e can\u2019t be salvaged?</div> </div> </div> </div>Man... it's difficult, as Gale himself put it, the moment to make the fifth editions take off was when V5 launched, but what they did was divide the public and frankly W5 doesn't seem to be very different, I don't think it was made to please the the old WTA audience at least, you may not think so, but the point is that at the very least it divided and even if it changes they will hardly be able to remove this image that caused displeasure among some of the fans, just with a lot of work and time. That said, it wouldn't be impossible, but it would require a lot of work that no one is willing to do nowadays, so the remaining options would be to continue with what they've already done, or freeze the WOD for a few years and suppose they will do the first. Ironically W5 will be a lot of people's first contact with WTA so it would eventually be the new official one, I don't know if many people coming in now would bother looking for the old editions or even care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T05:20:05-08:00","id":1525958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525921#post1525921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It IS just a soulless money grab.<br /> I am willing to die on that hill<br /> You know why the Chicago by Night 5th Edition and its supplements or anything basically Onyx Path Publishing made was a HUGE success?<br /> <i>Kickstarter</i>\u200b<br /> Becasue everything they made was made <i>for the gamers</i>, gave them <i>what they want for their money,</i> not showed everything and the kitchen sink Paradox <i>decided</i> the players want down their throath - or at least tried - and failed misreably<br /> But tried to grab as much cash as inhumanly possible nontheless and still not willing to admit their mistakes and pumping out 5th edition didasters after disasters</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> RPG companies at the end are still companies, and have to make money. The IP acquisition was motivated of course by the idea that they would make a &quot;Cyberpunk 2077&quot; move with Bloodlines 2, but the Paradox CEO of the time was also a long-time gamer of WOD, and personally invested in the setting. <div align=\"right\">\u200b</div> <br /> <br /> The treadmill of the 90s too could be called a money grab, and it gave us a very deep setting. It wasn't soulless.<br /> <br /> The Wod20 editions could be called a money grab based on nostalgia as well. But they were works of love, gave us updated setting and rules, and restarted the classic Wod. They weren't soulless.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> As for the gamer argument ... Martin Ericsson is a gamer, Jason Carl is a gamer, Outstar is a gamer, they all are gamers. It is also frequently forgotten that Matthew Dawkins and OPP freelancers worked a lot on V5, and that Matthew was Creative Lead Designer for a while and its basically firsty brand ambassador, as the Gentleman Gamer.<br /> <br /> And yet, Wod5e took their risks in changing rules and metaplot. Had it been soulless, it would have looked much different and more conservative. Wod5e was realized by gamers and long time fans, helped by experienced game designers and historical authors and freelancers. Had it been a soulless money grab showing everything down the troath of old time fans, they wouldn't have started the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> That said, editorially speaking, Wod5e is not a disaster: it has re-entered icv2 charts various times, coming in the top5, and it has wide international distribution agreements. It's also doing fairly well on Drivethrurpg. Kickstarter by Onyx Paths realized amazing products, whose reprint as physical editions has powerfully propelled Wod5e in the icv2 charts again, last Fall: but had not been for Paradox deals and Renegade distribution, they would just have stayed wonderful books acquired by ... 1000 or so Kickstarter backers, and later on an equivalent number of people on Drivethrurpg.<br /> <br /> To get my italian V20 distribution back again, another publishing house had to publish V5 ... and this propelled back interest in the franchise and moved the other publisher to print more V20 books.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, the WOD is widely available in a huge number of countries, languages and publishing formats, and also supports extensive fan modding. This, by itself, it's awesome.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Wod5e has failed in many of its original ambitions (uniting fandom, having a Cyberpunk 2077 moment, having a Dnd 5e big recognition...), and even though commercially speaking is doing well, it's just a sidenote on Paradox balance sheets.<br /> <br /> This, I think, is sad, missed chance: for a brief moment we had important designers, committed fans, long-time stewards of the franchise, and an international distribution network with huge transmedia ambitions working together to bring the Wod to its formery glory. It didn't work as intended.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 11-26-2023, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T11:43:11-08:00","id":1525969,"title":"","content":"Maybe I\u2019m in the minority, but I do like the idea of having blood potency in the Vampire The Masquerade setting if nothing else that even those of the same generation would have thicker blood and weakness as they get older and find the feeding requirements harder to meet and put themselves further down there road of becoming horrible monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T13:23:09-08:00","id":1525975,"title":"","content":"VtM with more variation within each Generation beyond age/XP would be good for VtM. The implementation of porting Blood Potency from VtR and trying to mesh it with Generation is too messy.<br /> <br /> I'd rather see something like how Roads/Paths worked: have a trade off of higher power (Aura bonuses) for more restrictions (more actions require checks to avoid dropping your rating) that would layer more smoothly on top of Generation would have less complaints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T13:58:41-08:00","id":1525977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525958#post1525958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> RPG companies at the end are still companies, and have to make money. The IP acquisition was motivated of course by the idea that they would make a &quot;Cyberpunk 2077&quot; move with Bloodlines 2, but the Paradox CEO of the time was also a long-time gamer of WOD, and personally invested in the setting. <div align=\"right\">\u200b</div><br /> <br /> The treadmill of the 90s too could be called a money grab, and it gave us a very deep setting. It wasn't soulless.<br /> <br /> The Wod20 editions could be called a money grab based on nostalgia as well. But they were works of love, gave us updated setting and rules, and restarted the classic Wod. They weren't soulless.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> As for the gamer argument ... Martin Ericsson is a gamer, Jason Carl is a gamer, Outstar is a gamer, they all are gamers. It is also frequently forgotten that Matthew Dawkins and OPP freelancers worked a lot on V5, and that Matthew was Creative Lead Designer for a while and its basically firsty brand ambassador, as the Gentleman Gamer.<br /> <br /> And yet, Wod5e took their risks in changing rules and metaplot. Had it been soulless, it would have looked much different and more conservative. Wod5e was realized by gamers and long time fans, helped by experienced game designers and historical authors and freelancers. Had it been a soulless money grab showing everything down the troath of old time fans, they wouldn't have started the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> That said, editorially speaking, Wod5e is not a disaster: it has re-entered icv2 charts various times, coming in the top5, and it has wide international distribution agreements. It's also doing fairly well on Drivethrurpg. Kickstarter by Onyx Paths realized amazing products, whose reprint as physical editions has powerfully propelled Wod5e in the icv2 charts again, last Fall: but had not been for Paradox deals and Renegade distribution, they would just have stayed wonderful books acquired by ... 1000 or so Kickstarter backers, and later on an equivalent number of people on Drivethrurpg.<br /> <br /> To get my italian V20 distribution back again, another publishing house had to publish V5 ... and this propelled back interest in the franchise and moved the other publisher to print more V20 books.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, the WOD is widely available in a huge number of countries, languages and publishing formats, and also supports extensive fan modding. This, by itself, it's awesome.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Wod5e has failed in many of its original ambitions (uniting fandom, having a Cyberpunk 2077 moment, having a Dnd 5e big recognition...), and even though commercially speaking is doing well, it's just a sidenote on Paradox balance sheets.<br /> <br /> This, I think, is sad, missed chance: for a brief moment we had important designers, committed fans, long-time stewards of the franchise, and an international distribution network with huge transmedia ambitions working together to bring the Wod to its formery glory. It didn't work as intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think the bottom-line of all of that what you described here is: WOD5E has failed.<br /> <br /> The main-reason for that is that saying &quot;It didn't work as intended.&quot; is one thing but what happens in response is another. Sure, shit happens, WOD5E had its shit-show moments - so how do Paradox/Renegade plan to turn things around? One move was establishing that in-house-team and prioritizing Renegade for supplements. Seemed like a good idea back then. But Justin Achilli, the designated lead-developer, has left and Renegade's ability as a distributor has hit a snafu leading to delays (which could just be a temporary thing - but what if it isn't...?). And there's no strategy here beyond &quot;Just trust us.&quot; right now. Can Renegade truly keep up with the publishing-schedule Paradox expects of them? Who is even in charge of developing the next corebook in WOD5E?<br /> <br /> One of the main-reasons I think WOD5E has failed is that there was a great moment with the release of V5 to actually make WOD5E a big thing and then that opportunity got squandered. Sure, that wasn't great but you can turn things around - and yet the history of WOD5E so far only becomes noticeable in the public eye when it adds yet another piece of bad writing to its seemingly ever-burning pyre of shame. It really has only gone downhill from there. People care about the V5 Corebook - but that's about it. I doubt it was mere greed that moved Renegade to give WOD5E books that hefty price-tag. It isn't Renegade's fault that shipping-prices are where they are but is Renegade actually still able to be the kind of distributor it used to be? I guess, we'll see just how bad things are with Renegade and if they managed to recover. As per the plans that were presented at the start of the year, Renegade is behind schedule. They claim their current problems will get resolved and therefore at the start of the coming year physical releases of all sorts will happen at the same time. Don't think that's a good idea but here we are. I guess we're gonna see when the first quartal of 2024 comes around. Theoretically, this will see the physical release of five WOD5E supplements in Q1 2024 according to the current schedule. Together with the hefty Renegade-price-tag, this doesn't sound like a good strategy.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T15:12:41-08:00","id":1525983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525958#post1525958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> RPG companies at the end are still companies, and have to make money. The IP acquisition was motivated of course by the idea that they would make a &quot;Cyberpunk 2077&quot; move with Bloodlines 2, but the Paradox CEO of the time was also a long-time gamer of WOD, and personally invested in the setting. <div align=\"right\">\u200b</div><br /> <br /> The treadmill of the 90s too could be called a money grab, and it gave us a very deep setting. It wasn't soulless.<br /> <br /> The Wod20 editions could be called a money grab based on nostalgia as well. But they were works of love, gave us updated setting and rules, and restarted the classic Wod. They weren't soulless.<br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> As for the gamer argument ... Martin Ericsson is a gamer, Jason Carl is a gamer, Outstar is a gamer, they all are gamers. It is also frequently forgotten that Matthew Dawkins and OPP freelancers worked a lot on V5, and that Matthew was Creative Lead Designer for a while and its basically firsty brand ambassador, as the Gentleman Gamer.<br /> <br /> And yet, Wod5e took their risks in changing rules and metaplot. Had it been soulless, it would have looked much different and more conservative. Wod5e was realized by gamers and long time fans, helped by experienced game designers and historical authors and freelancers. Had it been a soulless money grab showing everything down the troath of old time fans, they wouldn't have started the Storytellers Vault.<br /> <br /> That said, editorially speaking, Wod5e is not a disaster: it has re-entered icv2 charts various times, coming in the top5, and it has wide international distribution agreements. It's also doing fairly well on Drivethrurpg. Kickstarter by Onyx Paths realized amazing products, whose reprint as physical editions has powerfully propelled Wod5e in the icv2 charts again, last Fall: but had not been for Paradox deals and Renegade distribution, they would just have stayed wonderful books acquired by ... 1000 or so Kickstarter backers, and later on an equivalent number of people on Drivethrurpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>The crowdfunding successes seem like they're going to be things of the past. Also, out of the top5, it's a long, long way down from 1 to 2, and WoD isn't even there. It is, at best, #2, behind both D&amp;D and notD&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To get my italian V20 distribution back again, another publishing house had to publish V5 ... and this propelled back interest in the franchise and moved the other publisher to print more V20 books.<br /> <br /> Nowadays, the WOD is widely available in a huge number of countries, languages and publishing formats, and also supports extensive fan modding. This, by itself, it's awesome. </div> </div> </div>In what way does WoD5 support fan modding? It starts with an &quot;our way or the highway&quot; core book, and any modding you do is off the beaten path and likely considered to be badwrong fun by the creative lead. There's a nice repository for it, but it's still going to be a fair bit of work to apply it because WoD5 shares D&amp;D5's abandonment of writer responsibility, leaving STs as hung out to dry as most DMs are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Unfortunately, Wod5e has failed in many of its original ambitions (uniting fandom, having a Cyberpunk 2077 moment, having a Dnd 5e big recognition...), and even though commercially speaking is doing well, it's just a sidenote on Paradox balance sheets.<br /> <br /> This, I think, is sad, missed chance: for a brief moment we had important designers, committed fans, long-time stewards of the franchise, and an international distribution network with huge transmedia ambitions working together to bring the Wod to its formery glory. It didn't work as intended. </div> </div> </div>With the people they stuck at the top, hope was never a thing that anyone could have, unless they, too, were die-hard Vampire-maining LARPists that considered everything else an afterthought that they could roll in and steam over to great fanfare, like that isekai where the cast can't go five minutes without clapping for the protagonist doing anything with his cool powers.<br /> <br /> But life isn't that power fantasy, so there are at least some rotting fruits and vegetables with that applause for turning the Get of Fenris into Remnants of Despair. Assuming anyone did applaud that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T17:52:36-08:00","id":1525985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525983#post1525983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But life isn't that power fantasy, so there are at least some rotting fruits and vegetables with that applause for turning the Get of Fenris into Remnants of Despair. Assuming anyone did applaud that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, have, I can guarantee.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-26T18:52:37-08:00","id":1525990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525985#post1525985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, have, I can guarantee.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>People must really be desperate for new Danganronpa if they're going to W:tA for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T03:43:30-08:00","id":1525997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525862#post1525862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the main thing. Yeah, VtM is a whole social impact. And VtR is great in their own right. But they don't intermingle. V5 is a tragedy because they tried to hammer VtR mechanics in VtM lore, and, really? No, just no. If the Requiem mechanics are to be praised, keep the line going, AS REQUIEM. Because mashing the universes just don't work. The main complaints against V5 (and, frankly, I'll engross the choir) are the VtR things that were willy nilly trounced in VtM. So, again, if Requiem is accepted, publish Requiem, if Masquerade wants to keep going, it must keep going as Masquerade, not this szlatcha of systems. Fans of Requiem are happy, fans of Masquerade are happy, the sales go up. Would be the best solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 has nothing to do with CHAD Requiem<br /> <br /> They did not mash anything, Requiem 2ED/Blood and Smoke &amp; Danse Macabre is just Amazing from the game design perspective as it has multiple mechanics to allow you to: PLAY HOWEVER YOU WANT.<br /> <br /> ELDERS in Requiem are way more scary than those of the masquerade EX: Jurgen, Zagreus, The unholy, The Eyeless Mother Etc...<br /> <br /> Requiem is basically a toolbox full of optional mechanics to personalize your own experience and help you create whatever game you prefer. They openly talk about different power tiers from street level to Global conspiracies.<br /> <br /> V5 is the opposite, it is a restrictive system that works according to your horoscope and with a really bad writting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T06:10:20-08:00","id":1525998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525940#post1525940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How would this work?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanic = Requiem 2\u00b0 Edition<br /> Adaptation = Clans, disciplines and banes<br /> Lore = Beckett Jyhad Diary book 2 (conclusion and unification of new and old metaplot)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T08:55:39-08:00","id":1526008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525990#post1525990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People must really be desperate for new Danganronpa if they're going to W:tA for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more along the lines that some people have always seen the GOF that way and the W5 just &quot;took them out of the closet&quot; and a few other rather unpleasant things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T09:18:03-08:00","id":1526009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526008#post1526008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more along the lines that some people have always seen the GOF that way and the W5 just &quot;took them out of the closet&quot; and a few other rather unpleasant things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's one goal for WoD5, I guess - stop bringing back previously-killed Nazi splinter groups of a splat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-27T11:02:46-08:00","id":1526014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525998#post1525998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mechanic = Requiem 2\u00b0 Edition<br /> Adaptation = Clans, disciplines and banes<br /> Lore = Beckett Jyhad Diary book 2 (conclusion and unification of new and old metaplot)</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically Masquiem, there is even a traslation guide allowing people to mix the games mechanics and lore. The requiem homebrew hub also has a lot of ports. <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulisses</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525834#post1525834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good Lord, Vampire The Requiem 2th is the best vampire tabletop game made, my real dream? Take Rosa Bailey and Matthew Dawnkins em give them total criative control to create Vampire The Masquerade 6\u00b0 edition (with base rules of VtR 2th adaptation to Masquerade scenario)<br /> <br /> Forget V5<br /> <br /> This is the perfect world for all fandom of Vampire rpg.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I think Rose Baley work so far has been top tier, however Mattew Dawkins has been one of most prominent figures of V5<br /> <br /> The few requiem and onix path books that i do not like have him as a writter, developer or another prominent role with traces of what to me start to resemble what would become V5<br /> <br /> To me Mattew = More V5 and I do not want that <hr /><br /> That said who the line developer is does not matter as long as Paradox is the owner of VTM. They have seen many failures with the line and decided to still keep doing the same, only changing the frontman, promising to not do it again like a toxic boyfriend who repeats the same actions while victim blaming the GF.<br /> <br /> Hell the idea to reducing the number of clans to 7 and sell the rest in DLCs resembles the way they sell their games (One basic core game + many DLC that allow you the full experience)<br /> <br /> The random events that happen in their games also resemble a lot the intruding Hunger Dice, Compulsions etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 11-27-2023, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T03:33:55-08:00","id":1526046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1525997#post1525997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 has nothing to do with CHAD Requiem<br /> <br /> They did not mash anything, Requiem 2ED/Blood and Smoke &amp; Danse Macabre is just Amazing from the game design perspective as it has multiple mechanics to allow you to: PLAY HOWEVER YOU WANT</div> </div> </div> </div>Since when blood potency, touchstones, streamlined disciplines and multiple disciplines per level are part of VtM, or even viable? Because I remember that, better done and lore sensible on the Requiem. Not so much on the Masquerade. So, yeah, I'll keep telling that V5 took VtR mechanics and threw on VtM carelessly. And that was bad to the Masquerade because is inconsistent, and is bad for Requiem, because there's no reason to continue since V5 is fusing both, so, no more material.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T05:31:46-08:00","id":1526053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526046#post1526046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Since when blood potency, touchstones, streamlined disciplines and multiple disciplines per level are part of VtM, or even viable? Because I remember that, better done and lore sensible on the Requiem. Not so much on the Masquerade. So, yeah, I'll keep telling that V5 took VtR mechanics and threw on VtM carelessly. And that was bad to the Masquerade because is inconsistent, and is bad for Requiem, because there's no reason to continue since V5 is fusing both, so, no more material.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree that V5 is bad for both Requiem and VTM. That said:<br /> <br /> Blood Potency, Touchstones, and Devotions/disciplines in requiem operate TOTALLY different to their equivalent in V5.<ul><li>Touchstones can be objects and are optional</li> <li>Humanity uses breaking points, not convictions or tenets</li> <li>Basic discipline levels are extremely versatile and customizable even without adding devotions just read their write up of protean: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1juI7Er1pUnl79v9zt8NCu4q6jynnCGKJvMZwHJHot7s/pub\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...MZwHJHot7s/pub</a></li> <li>Blood Potency is an enormous buff in Requiem it allows absurd dicepools, it also does not have generations, has more clean mechanics and opens more plot points because some elders enter in torpor to lower it while others refuse to do it becoming predators among predators (possible blood hunt).</li> </ul><br /> Not to mention that those concepts where already in VTM. Ex: Devotions = Combo disciplines + LV9-10 powers or true love merit etc... requiem just perfected them and this is one of the reasons why people use the translation guide to masquerade with requiem rules. So yes they are extremely compatible.<br /> <br /> <b><u>In V5 those mechanics only share the name, as they operate under completely different rules. Hence there is no point of comparing.</u></b><br /> <br /> Is like comparing an actual Ferrari (Requiem) with the toy version (V5) because they both are named Ferrari, however they are not the same.<br /> <br /> It is completely unfair to discredit requiem like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T07:02:17-08:00","id":1526061,"title":"","content":"And that's what I'm saying, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a> . Is unfair this mash up. And that's a pretty common complain, they took Requiem mechanics and used in a bizarre way in V5. They work in Requiem because they're well thought and made to work and work in the scenario. V5 tried to take that and failed miserably because there are two different systems with two different premises. The paper a Methuselah is supposed to do in the Masquerade and the paper a high blood potency vampire is supposed to do in the Requiem are different. On the Masquerade, the low generation are an unavoidable threat, dealed differently between the highly hierarchical Camarilla and the way more &quot;caothic&quot; Sabbath. On the Requiem the threat is different, because you can voluntarily go in a torpor to drop your blood potency. You can't go from a lower to a higher generation because that would break the system. The fear of Gehenna is a vital part of the Masquerade. The fear of a 2k yo on Requiem is just not the same. It hit differently because he can be recently awakened of a volunteer torpor to be functional again. The blood thins with torpors, which is not supposed to happen in the Masquerade. Caine is a sword in the neck of every single vampire in Masquerade. There ain't a First Vampire on Requiem, despite of what the Lance of Longuinius and the Circle of the Crone may say. A vampire that knew the Christ that awakens in the Masquerade and the Requiem hit differently, because in the Masquerade is a blood hungry demigod that can wipe NY with a thought while in the Requiem may be a very cultivated low potency guy that can be lying through their fangs with bizarre memories that may or may not be real. The awakening of Ur-Shulgi remodeled the Banu Hakim formerly known as Assamites. The awakening of a vampire of same age that spent as long in torpor in the Requiem is just not the same. There are different games, which must be played differently, and throwing things as blood potency in the Masquerade is both ridiculous and counterproductive. Someone as Montano can't happen in the Requiem with very good reasons, because the scenario don't allow. A Gratiano in the Requiem wouldn't have the power to absolutely change, let's say, the Mekhet, because a Gratiano just can't happen in the Requiem. As I said, they're both good games with different premises, and trying to put mechanics of one in the other (blood potency, by chance) is not functional. That's the gist of what I'm trying to say. (Sorry for any misspellings, I just can't put trough/through/throughout in my head)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-28T16:57:51-08:00","id":1526089,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a revised sourcebook on how Kindred can gain influence in mortal society and some in industries that most people wouldn't think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T02:45:55-08:00","id":1526108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526061#post1526061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that's what I'm saying, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24037_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24037\" data-vbnamecard=\"24037\">Leandro16</a> . Is unfair this mash up. And that's a pretty common complain, they took Requiem mechanics and used in a bizarre way in V5. They work in Requiem because they're well thought and made to work and work in the scenario. V5 tried to take that and failed miserably because there are two different systems with two different premises. The paper a Methuselah is supposed to do in the Masquerade and the paper a high blood potency vampire is supposed to do in the Requiem are different. On the Masquerade, the low generation are an unavoidable threat, dealed differently between the highly hierarchical Camarilla and the way more &quot;caothic&quot; Sabbath. On the Requiem the threat is different, because you can voluntarily go in a torpor to drop your blood potency. You can't go from a lower to a higher generation because that would break the system. The fear of Gehenna is a vital part of the Masquerade. The fear of a 2k yo on Requiem is just not the same. It hit differently because he can be recently awakened of a volunteer torpor to be functional again. The blood thins with torpors, which is not supposed to happen in the Masquerade. Caine is a sword in the neck of every single vampire in Masquerade. There ain't a First Vampire on Requiem, despite of what the Lance of Longuinius and the Circle of the Crone may say. A vampire that knew the Christ that awakens in the Masquerade and the Requiem hit differently, because in the Masquerade is a blood hungry demigod that can wipe NY with a thought while in the Requiem may be a very cultivated low potency guy that can be lying through their fangs with bizarre memories that may or may not be real. The awakening of Ur-Shulgi remodeled the Banu Hakim formerly known as Assamites. The awakening of a vampire of same age that spent as long in torpor in the Requiem is just not the same. There are different games, which must be played differently, and throwing things as blood potency in the Masquerade is both ridiculous and counterproductive. Someone as Montano can't happen in the Requiem with very good reasons, because the scenario don't allow. A Gratiano in the Requiem wouldn't have the power to absolutely change, let's say, the Mekhet, because a Gratiano just can't happen in the Requiem. As I said, they're both good games with different premises, and trying to put mechanics of one in the other (blood potency, by chance) is not functional. That's the gist of what I'm trying to say. (Sorry for any misspellings, I just can't put trough/through/throughout in my head)</div> </div> </div> </div>In Requiem 2.000 Years + Vampires are stronger than the antediluvians<ul><li><b>Zagreus</b> has basically Dominate 10, he can make a wish and his mastery of dominate is so strong that he would subconsciusly guide the actions of people to make it happen. without even being in the same place. This is described as introducing plot elements, in other words Zagreus dominate is so powerful that he behaves as the narrator. And there is mechanics for this. Such is the beuty of requiem.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Dorjan </b>is one with his land. He can see everything within it, blood bond anyone who enters it, manifest on every part of it as a ghost etc... Joke is he is getting stronger and has still not reached his peak. Within few years his range will grow to control the whole metropolithan area of Budapest. He might not even be a methusaleah and instead be an unusually powerful elder.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>The Sighless Mother or La Llorona</b> is a living discipline the incarnation of blood sorcery, she could wipe up the dust with Tzimisce, she does not even have flesh to manipulate, she is made out of ephemera. Her dominance of blood magic makes her a plot device.</li> </ul><br /> Requiem Elders even depowered by torpor which is also canon in masquerade (Ask Helena and Menele) keep their disciplines and stats above 5, not to mention that they have mediums like the coils of the dragon and devotions to work around. Some don\u00b4t weaken at all, others can still fight at antediluvians levels. Hell elders in requiem have feat that put them in Methusaleah range like Hecate, Jurgen etc... They are monsters so powerful that they can be considerated something else. All this without counting patron spirits from Mage or Werewolf who are upper dimensional beings and would see the antediluvians as babies.<br /> <br /> I understand that you are not familiar with requiem, and the idea that you have of the game steems from the first edition core book where everything was more of a sketch, than the fineshed product it is today. Today requiem is not a street level game, it is a whatever power level you want it to be as a Storyteller, that is why everyone describes it as a toolbox and praises it\u00b4s mechanics/rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/cicerondixit/gallery</a>","edited":{"userid":24037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","user":"Leandro16","date":". 11-29-2023, 08:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24037-leandro16","name":"Leandro16","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24037_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T05:33:40-08:00","id":1526109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leandro16</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526108#post1526108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In Requiem 2.000 Years + Vampires are stronger than the antediluvians<ul><li><b>Zagreus</b> has basically Dominate 10, he can make a wish and his mastery of dominate is so strong that he would subconsciusly guide the actions of people to make it happen. without even being in the same place. This is described as introducing plot elements, in other words Zagreus dominate is so powerful that he behaves as the narrator. And there is mechanics for this. Such is the beuty of requiem.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>Dorjan </b>is one with his land. He can see everything within it, blood bond anyone who enters it, manifest on every part of it as a ghost etc... Joke is he is getting stronger and has still not reached his peak. Within few years his range will grow to control the whole metropolithan area of Budapest. He might not even be a methusaleah and instead be an unusually powerful elder.</li> </ul><ul><li><b>The Sighless Mother or La Llorona</b> is a living discipline the incarnation of blood sorcery, she could wipe up the dust with Tzimisce, she does not even have flesh to manipulate, she is made out of ephemera. Her dominance of blood magic makes her a plot device.</li> </ul><br /> Requiem Elders even depowered by torpor which is also canon in masquerade (Ask Helena and Menele) keep their disciplines and stats above 5, not to mention that they have mediums like the coils of the dragon and devotions to work around. Some don\u00b4t weaken at all, others can still fight at antediluvians levels. Hell elders in requiem have feat that put them in Methusaleah range like Hecate, Jurgen etc... They are monsters so powerful that they can be considerated something else. All this without counting patron spirits from Mage or Werewolf who are upper dimensional beings and would see the antediluvians as babies.<br /> <br /> I understand that you are not familiar with requiem, and the idea that you have of the game steems from the first edition core book where everything was more of a sketch, than the fineshed product it is today. Today requiem is not a street level game, it is a whatever power level you want it to be as a Storyteller, that is why everyone describes it as a toolbox and praises it\u00b4s mechanics/rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's me guessing, but I think that in VTM, Zagreus would be the Ventrue antidiluvian or related to the same, you could even say that he diablerized him or that in fact everyone thinks he is dead because he wanted like that using his discipline level 10, or if you want an interesting plot you can think of something similar to what happens to the Brujah, it would be more interesting than just considering him dead; Dorjan, I think that unlike an antidiluvian he would be more of a methuselah of the Tzimice or Gangrel clan, instead of connecting with his land he would merge with it, there are Tzimice elders who can do this with an entire room so it's to be expected thinking that it would be possible to do more with more power, but the antidiluvians would do it on a global scale; Llorona I think such a creature would be better off as an unknown member of the second generation so she observes the Jyhad, but does not interfere., so her only direct threat would be Cain or perhaps an angel; For the record, I didn't read about them, it just came to mind based on your description.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T10:46:10-08:00","id":1526121,"title":"","content":"Indeed the one big thing I liked about VTR was that given enough time a Kindred could reach anti status, but the feeding requirements would be hard to meet as how would a Mekhet that is equal to a member of the fifth generation be able to keep kindred snacks around?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T17:46:39-08:00","id":1526143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526121#post1526121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed the one big thing I liked about VTR was that given enough time a Kindred could reach anti status, but the feeding requirements would be hard to meet as how would a Mekhet that is equal to a member of the fifth generation be able to keep kindred snacks around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Invictus Blood Oaths, specifically the Oath of Serfdom. It's a big part of why the Invictus is the covenant for elders, use your connections and power to claim territory, then collect red rent from younger kindred while the oath protects you from the blood bond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-29T18:41:02-08:00","id":1526148,"title":"","content":"I want V5 to finally be discontinued and the metaplot scrapped<br /> <br /> Sadly won't ever happen so long as Paradox owns the IP. Hopefully Bloodlines 2 failing will be more than enough of a consolation prize for that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T03:44:54-08:00","id":1526173,"title":"","content":"V:tM has never <i>quite</i> conjured associations of approachable mechanics, so I'm simultaneously sympathetic to any calls for simplification (something V5 does not even aim to achieve by importing a totally unrelated system on top of V:tM's own system) and forgiving of failures to untagle the mess that is <i>Masquerade</i>'s game design; what I find significantly less forgivable is the fact V5 didn't even have the decency to compensate for failures in game design by making itself a <i>work of art</i>, which has been the line's modus operandi since day one. The evocativeness and sincerity of classic V:tM justify investing in it even if one doesn't intend to make use of it as a TTRPG system; it is very hard for me to believe this level of artistic merit will be recognised in V5 three decades from now. Do people truly find more offence in misguided candor and unrepentant adolescent sincerity than in vapid self-referentiality and a pathological fear of vulnerability? Are katana-wielding vampires dressed in leather trench coats truly more distasteful than having a<i> TTRPG</i> <i>in which you roleplay as a vampire in modern Milwaukee</i> school you on the latest Drumpf tweet fail?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to &quot;defend&quot; the worst excesses of V:tM/cWoD (though I maintain tone-deafness is in basically all cases preferable to insincerity). I'm saying there's still a stable consumer base of overly sincere social rejects to whom an updated, streamlined version of classic <i>Masquerade</i> (that maintains the artistic trappings of the original) would appeal to, and who maintain a right to creative expression without having to justify their weirdness in reference to the latest asinine concern of mainstream culture. V5 succeeded to the extent it managed to engage those to whom the conceits of <i>Masquerade</i> appeal to; I would quite like for any future edition of <i>Masquerade</i> to abstain from appeals to mainstream sensibilities in the pursuit of a fresh coat of paint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-30T11:16:19-08:00","id":1526189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526143#post1526143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Invictus Blood Oaths, specifically the Oath of Serfdom. It's a big part of why the Invictus is the covenant for elders, use your connections and power to claim territory, then collect red rent from younger kindred while the oath protects you from the blood bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could work, but if said Mekhet was a member of the unaligned groups, that could be tricky to do unless the local Prince has worked out a deal with the elder or ancient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T04:47:20-08:00","id":1526199,"title":"","content":"For the entire WoD line to be put to bed and maybe revisited in 10+ years from now. We're in an artistic dark age right now where every form of expression from movies, TV, Video games, and Tabletop are all being horribly mismanaged by companies and &quot;writers&quot; too disconnected from reality to understand that they're burning their own house down.<br /> <br /> After seeing what's happened to other beloved franchises from the pre-2000's, I don't think the industry as a whole is in any position to course-correct. I think allowing some series to just End, maybe forever, might be for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-01T15:02:37-08:00","id":1526212,"title":"","content":"Not forever, but a nice break to reset the creative batteries would work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T06:17:17-08:00","id":1526514,"title":"","content":"This is going to sound potentially not too profound, but I sincerely wish to see high levels of play being more common or at last available. I cannot stress just how tedious and monotonous it is to constantly be chained to the standard character creation rules (whether V20 or V5) and having the standard sects in play. It is as if nothing changes and everyone is terrified to step out of the box of generic play.<br /> <br /> The most common opposing opinion I hear of this that it is potentially &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;too OP&quot;, which is simply not the case. Anyone who has played Mage, Changeling, or even Werewolf knows how to properly adjust the scope and difficulty of the game to reflect a deeper form of play.<br /> <br /> I don't say this because I dislike more &quot;street-level&quot; games. I have had characters I absolutely love who are part of the street-level tier of play and have made stories involving such characters that I've been very invested in...but when I do it again for the, what, tenth time, I become so incredibly bored very quickly.<br /> <br /> I would love a book for VtM along the lines of Danse Macabre of VtR that delves into various levels of play and non-standard characters. A favorite trope of mine is having a low-generation character with an elder or even methuselah sire. I truly love the gothic atmosphere that that pairing evokes; being a young vampire so closely associated to an ancient being; being completely in over your head. Throw in even highly toxic/possessive romance, if you will, and you have quite an interesting character. I love playing elders especially becuase I love th existential crises, having a fully realized backstory to know where you stand in the world- there are just so many flavorful and interesting angles to play, if only these were actual options.<br /> <br /> I want to experience more sects as well. My favorite sect (besides the Camarilla) is the True Black Hand and, divisive as they are, are one of the most fascinating sects in the game for me. They cover so much of what I love about Vampire and yet, they are often shunned. Much of the same is said of the Inconnu as well, another favorite. Even the higher echolons of the Camarilla are often never touched upon. The only character I ever had that was even close to a higher tier Camarilla character was a Malkavian ancilla on the path of becoming an Archon for the Malkavian justicar.<br /> <br /> I do confess that I tend to play in play-by-post Discords and one forum, so those venues tend to be highly restrictive. I've had less than stellar experience with table games in that they have fallen apart rather quickly, so investing my time wisely is very important to me.<br /> <br /> The tedium got to me so much that I eventually made my own private server focused on such higher tier characters with the other sects available, though personal life and minimal support (though I'm still grateful for it) led to me putting it on hibernate.<br /> <br /> Disclaimer: I do know (and own) the particular VtM book that helps with this, Elysium: The Elder Wars, the V20 True Black Hand Book, and have copies of the Guide to the Camarilla, Dread Names, Red List, and Council of Primogen. Almost none of these are ever utilized, sadly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2204,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","user":"Toreador","date":". 12-08-2023, 09:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T10:55:38-08:00","id":1526519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toreador</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526514#post1526514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to sound potentially not too profound, but I sincerely wish to see high levels of play being more common or at last available. I cannot stress just how tedious and monotonous it is to constantly be chained to the standard character creation rules (whether V20 or V5) and having the standard sects in play. It is as if nothing changes and everyone is terrified to step out of the box of generic play.<br /> <br /> The most common opposing opinion I hear of this that it is potentially &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;too OP&quot;, which is simply not the case. Anyone who has played Mage, Changeling, or even Werewolf knows how to properly adjust the scope and difficulty of the game to reflect a deeper form of play.<br /> <br /> I don't say this because I dislike more &quot;street-level&quot; games. I have had characters I absolutely love who are part of the street-level tier of play and have made stories involving such characters that I've been very invested in...but when I do it again for the, what, tenth time, I become so incredibly bored very quickly.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't agree more. <br /> <br /> The last few years, I've grown to think that people developing the WOD, either 20th or v5, don't know how to deal with medium to high level play, even in fictions. It first become apparent to me after listening to podcast with Phil brucato (mage being my favorite wod game) and seeing how he constantly advocate for low ar\u00eate/sph\u00e8re games. <br /> <br /> Then you look at the 20th anniversary short stories entologies. Which, while indeed of good quality, are nearly all about low scale stories (the most flagrant for me was &quot;Truth beyond paradox&quot; where nearly all stories are of awakenings or initiate level mages). <br /> <br /> And this continue in the recent howl of the apocalypse supplement to apocalyptic record, this is supposed to be a book about plot directly linked to end of the world issues, and yet they are all local street level plots. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T12:37:20-08:00","id":1526524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toreador</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526514#post1526514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The most common opposing opinion I hear of this that it is potentially &quot;broken&quot; or &quot;too OP&quot;, which is simply not the case. Anyone who has played Mage, Changeling, or even Werewolf knows how to properly adjust the scope and difficulty of the game to reflect a deeper form of play.</div> </div> </div> </div>It weirds me out that so many people have this opinion, including the Current Game Designers, when one of the landmark titles of VTM that had it break into wider markets was the Video Game VTM: Redemption(the granddaddy of Bloodlines). In that game you play an <i>Elder's Rise to Power</i> through medieval to modern nights, and in which you <i>Kill A Methusela in Combat</i>(Christof may be high-gen for an elder, but Nobody is going to be questioning his title).<br /> <br /> I seriously don't think the current designers vision lines up with what made WoD popular <b>Before</b> the original Bloodlines came out. Bloodlines by itself wasn't what made WoD popular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T13:59:37-08:00","id":1526526,"title":"","content":"I guess Mage Revised was the one that fell the hardest. From the ones that could change reality at will to the poor, defenseless scared victims of the Avatar Storm, unable to access their strongest powers, with no guidance, since their umbral masters and oracles were cut from Earth, the Marauders were devastated, and even the omnipotent Technocracy were feeling the aftershocks of the fall of Doissetep and the Horizon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T16:00:07-08:00","id":1526534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526519#post1526519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I couldn't agree more.<br /> <br /> The last few years, I've grown to think that people developing the WOD, either 20th or v5, don't know how to deal with medium to high level play, even in fictions. It first become apparent to me after listening to podcast with Phil brucato (mage being my favorite wod game) and seeing how he constantly advocate for low ar\u00eate/sph\u00e8re games.<br /> <br /> Then you look at the 20th anniversary short stories entologies. Which, while indeed of good quality, are nearly all about low scale stories (the most flagrant for me was &quot;Truth beyond paradox&quot; where nearly all stories are of awakenings or initiate level mages).<br /> <br /> And this continue in the recent howl of the apocalypse supplement to apocalyptic record, this is supposed to be a book about plot directly linked to end of the world issues, and yet they are all local street level plots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Phil Brucato? The same man who was behind Mage 2e? That's quite funny, given how cosmic that edition was (and being the one that made me fall in love with Mage over Vampire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-08T16:00:26-08:00","id":1526535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526526#post1526526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess Mage Revised was the one that fell the hardest. From the ones that could change reality at will to the poor, defenseless scared victims of the Avatar Storm, unable to access their strongest powers, with no guidance, since their umbral masters and oracles were cut from Earth, the Marauders were devastated, and even the omnipotent Technocracy were feeling the aftershocks of the fall of Doissetep and the Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't sell the WoD5 development staff short. Mage could hit rock bottom again... and then proceed to dig further down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T05:57:03-08:00","id":1526594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526173#post1526173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V:tM has never <i>quite</i> conjured associations of approachable mechanics, so I'm simultaneously sympathetic to any calls for simplification (something V5 does not even aim to achieve by importing a totally unrelated system on top of V:tM's own system) and forgiving of failures to untagle the mess that is <i>Masquerade</i>'s game design; what I find significantly less forgivable is the fact V5 didn't even have the decency to compensate for failures in game design by making itself a <i>work of art</i>, which has been the line's modus operandi since day one. The evocativeness and sincerity of classic V:tM justify investing in it even if one doesn't intend to make use of it as a TTRPG system; it is very hard for me to believe this level of artistic merit will be recognised in V5 three decades from now. Do people truly find more offence in misguided candor and unrepentant adolescent sincerity than in vapid self-referentiality and a pathological fear of vulnerability? Are katana-wielding vampires dressed in leather trench coats truly more distasteful than having a<i> TTRPG</i> <i>in which you roleplay as a vampire in modern Milwaukee</i> school you on the latest Drumpf tweet fail?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to &quot;defend&quot; the worst excesses of V:tM/cWoD (though I maintain tone-deafness is in basically all cases preferable to insincerity). I'm saying there's still a stable consumer base of overly sincere social rejects to whom an updated, streamlined version of classic <i>Masquerade</i> (that maintains the artistic trappings of the original) would appeal to, and who maintain a right to creative expression without having to justify their weirdness in reference to the latest asinine concern of mainstream culture. V5 succeeded to the extent it managed to engage those to whom the conceits of <i>Masquerade</i> appeal to; I would quite like for any future edition of <i>Masquerade</i> to abstain from appeals to mainstream sensibilities in the pursuit of a fresh coat of paint.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. I've been buying vtm since 1992 but haven't gone near v5 for various reasons, including ludicrous modern day pandering. This is a game where players pretend to be undead blood sucking corpses FFS . Also, art work in earlier editions was awesome, photos of actors dressed up doesn't compare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T08:14:28-08:00","id":1526598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordOfAsh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526594#post1526594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. I've been buying vtm since 1992 but haven't gone near v5 for various reasons, including ludicrous modern day pandering.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't followed v5 but I've seen this sentiment a lot. What 'modern day pandering' is in the edition?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T09:42:44-08:00","id":1526601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526598#post1526598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't followed v5 but I've seen this sentiment a lot. What 'modern day pandering' is in the edition?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think the sort of pandering V5 likes to indulge in is only really an example of 'modern pandering' to the extent it is precisely the kind of philistine banality that allows for sentences like '[<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fiorenza_Savona\" target=\"_blank\">the vampire Prince of Mexico City</a>] is an ascending kingpin [...] moving up societal ranks through NGOs and the UN(!), [who] knows everyone worth controlling in the Davos elite(!!!)' to be published in print that appeals to modern sensibilities.<br /> <br /> My desire is not for the game to be 'apolitical' - it's for the politics (and the psychoanalysis, and the poetry) to naturally flow out of the <i>internal logic of the game</i>. It is very, very obvious what the individual components of the game's setting stand for, if interpreted as clear-cut analogies for real-world events and institutions, to the extent it'd be gauche to even ask what do the Camarilla and its Inner Circle, the Sabbat and the Anarch Revolts, the Jyhad and the impotent struggle of young vampires against their elders 'mean' - the metaphors involved are simply too obvious. V5 commits the crime of killing the fantasy (inexcusable for a TTRPG) by <i>saying</i> what it all means: the Sabbat is no longer about the tragedy of angry young men tearing a world too small for them down only to find themselves trapped within the exact same cycle of misdirected violence and paranoia - it's <i>Literally About</i> ISIS and Atomwaffen and incels (and why would <i>you</i> want to play a terrorist Nazi incel?). The Camarilla is no longer about the mediaeval courtly intrigue reflected in an average office meeting, or the youngest member of an international crime syndicate seeking to make a change within a system he was never even asked to join - it is literally, actually about the current composition of the US Senate (and why would <i>you</i> want to play fucking vampire Mitch McConnell?). And here I was thinking Stoker made Dracula a 'count' for the Dark Academia vibes; what's next, is vampiric bloodthirst going to be a metaphor for drug addiction?<br /> <br /> There's a sense in which this is not solely the fault of us currently living through a cultural dark age. V5 chose to import the fundamental conceit of <i>Requiem</i>, that you're playing a vampire in what is literally our world with vampires and werewolves and witches added - <i>Requiem</i> is, to an extent, best played if you're playing as if it was you that was Embraced. This is not how <i>Masquerade</i> works, nor is it how the <i>World of Darkness</i> itself works - the whole idea is that you're <i>not</i> playing in the real world, that the events depicted during a chronicle did not happen and could never happen; the setting is exaggerated and distorted in a way that makes its fictional nature obvious. Blurring the line between this 'world of impressions' and the real world is artistically tasteless at best, and dangerous at worst: there is no pack of Sabbat vampires behind the latest cartel murder, and your CEO is not the ghoul of the Ventrue Prince; V5 openly claims otherwise, and is all the worse for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","user":"gamiem","date":". 12-10-2023, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T10:13:39-08:00","id":1526603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526601#post1526601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blurring the line between this 'world of impressions' and the real world is artistically tasteless at best, and dangerous at worst: there is no pack of Sabbat vampires behind the latest cartel murder, and your CEO is not the ghoul of the Ventrue Prince; V5 openly claims otherwise, and is all the worse for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This line struck me because I personally felt like this was a big issue with classic VtM. Is the issue you're describing that the kind of inferred massive control over world events from prior editions is replaced with explicit ties to present day events/organizations? I remember some sort of hubub over a V5 book a few years ago explicitly discussing vampires taking advantage of the anti-gay purges in Chechnya, which seems like an example of what I think you're talking about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T10:18:52-08:00","id":1526604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrDrika</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526526#post1526526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess Mage Revised was the one that fell the hardest. From the ones that could change reality at will to the poor, defenseless scared victims of the Avatar Storm, unable to access their strongest powers, with no guidance, since their umbral masters and oracles were cut from Earth, the Marauders were devastated, and even the omnipotent Technocracy were feeling the aftershocks of the fall of Doissetep and the Horizon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeing the pummelling W5 did to WtA, I shudder to imagine what M5 will do to Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T10:20:27-08:00","id":1526605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526601#post1526601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the sort of pandering V5 likes to indulge in is only really an example of 'modern pandering' to the extent it is precisely the kind of philistine banality that allows for sentences like '[<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fiorenza_Savona\" target=\"_blank\">the vampire Prince of Mexico City</a>] is an ascending kingpin [...] moving up societal ranks through NGOs and the UN(!), [who] knows everyone worth controlling in the Davos elite(!!!)' to be published in print that appeals to modern sensibilities.<br /> <br /> My desire is not for the game to be 'apolitical' - it's for the politics (and the psychoanalysis, and the poetry) to naturally flow out of the <i>internal logic of the game</i>. It is very, very obvious what the individual components of the game's setting stand for, if interpreted as clear-cut analogies for real-world events and institutions, to the extent it'd be gauche to even ask what do the Camarilla and its Inner Circle, the Sabbat and the Anarch Revolts, the Jyhad and the impotent struggle of young vampires against their elders 'mean' - the metaphors involved are simply too obvious. V5 commits the crime of killing the fantasy (inexcusable for a TTRPG) by <i>saying</i> what it all means: the Sabbat is no longer about the tragedy of angry young men tearing a world too small for them down only to find themselves trapped within the exact same cycle of misdirected violence and paranoia - it's <i>Literally About</i> ISIS and Atomwaffen and incels (and why would <i>you</i> want to play a terrorist Nazi incel?). The Camarilla is no longer about the mediaeval courtly intrigue reflected in an average office meeting, or the youngest member of an international crime syndicate seeking to make a change within a system he was never even asked to join - it is literally, actually about the current composition of the US Senate (and why would <i>you</i> want to play fucking vampire Mitch McConnell?). And here I was thinking Stoker made Dracula a 'count' for the Dark Academia vibes; what's next, is vampiric bloodthirst going to be a metaphor for drug addiction?<br /> <br /> There's a sense in which this is not solely the fault of us currently living through a cultural dark age. V5 chose to import the fundamental conceit of <i>Requiem</i>, that you're playing a vampire in what is literally our world with vampires and werewolves and witches added - <i>Requiem</i> is, to an extent, best played if you're playing as if it was you that was Embraced. This is not how <i>Masquerade</i> works, nor is it how the <i>World of Darkness</i> itself works - the whole idea is that you're <i>not</i> playing in the real world, that the events depicted during a chronicle did not happen and could never happen; the setting is exaggerated and distorted in a way that makes its fictional nature obvious. Blurring the line between this 'world of impressions' and the real world is artistically tasteless at best, and dangerous at worst: there is no pack of Sabbat vampires behind the latest cartel murder, and your CEO is not the ghoul of the Ventrue Prince; V5 openly claims otherwise, and is all the worse for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's quite unpleasant when I stop to think about it, it almost seems like... conditioning, did I use the right word?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T10:22:02-08:00","id":1526606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526604#post1526604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seeing the pummelling W5 did to WtA, I shudder to imagine what M5 will do to Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>pummeling?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T11:16:35-08:00","id":1526615,"title":"","content":"I want more Dark Ages, either more for DAV20 or a new edition.<br /> Not gonna happen, but I can dream. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T11:45:43-08:00","id":1526617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526603#post1526603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> [This line struck me because I personally felt like this was a big issue with classic VtM. Is the issue you're describing that the kind of inferred massive control over world events from prior editions is replaced with explicit ties to present day events/organizations? I remember some sort of hubub over a V5 book a few years ago explicitly discussing vampires taking advantage of the anti-gay purges in Chechnya, which seems like an example of what I think you're talking about.]<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of it, yeah. YMMV, but I think cVtM/cWoD suffers from a different if related flaw: beyond the fact any depiction of a subject based entirely on impressions will necessarily other the subject being depicted (this is, in essence, the critique levelled at <i>Kindred of the East</i>), the impressions WoD chooses to construct its setting out of are specifically the <i>worst</i> <i>impressions</i> of the real world. Someone, I think on this very forum, once said WoD Chicago is best imagined as being exactly like the depiction of the real city on Fox News - the setting takes the worst, most othering, most degrading fantasies and turns them into fact, to the point of sometimes venturing into outright alternate history (I think it was <i>Rage Across New York</i> that stated more than one of the state's IRL green zone laws never got approved in WoD?). <i>Werewolf</i>, being perhaps the line to take the idea of a 'World of Darkness' most seriously, contains some of the most flagrant examples of paranoid fiction being treated as fact - everything to do with Pentex, for one. This is a world whose building blocks are the feverish delusions of Lawrence Pazder and Jack Chick.<br /> <br /> What salvaged what could've easily been an exercise in right-wing hysteria was the fact cWoD never presented itself as an honest depiction of reality. I've memory-holed the entire Chechnya incident, but yes, it's an example of a general tendecy that pervades the entire product. Classic<i> Masquerade</i>, as I understand it, preferred to think of vampires as part of the ambience rather than a direct cause of the state of the world (an idea outright denied in <i>Mexico City by Night</i>, in fact); a world so awful must have place for literal bloodsuckers, I suppose. It's in V5 that this boundary crashes: beyond the obvious dangers, I think the conflation of impression with fact is just extremely tasteless in a very banal, trite sense. If I wanted to read about 'Davos elites' literally sucking the blood of unsuspecting commoners in order to stave off mortality, I'd go on Twitter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28177-gamiem","name":"gamiem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T12:44:22-08:00","id":1526623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>literatzi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526598#post1526598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I haven't followed v5 but I've seen this sentiment a lot. What 'modern day pandering' is in the edition?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think Gamiems point about real world vs fiction is the crux of it for me. Its a game of horror where undead blood sucking corpses exist alongside zombies, ghosts, werewolves, cannibals and all sorts of other entities based in a world like our own but where horror is exaggerated and monsters exist. It takes a certain buy-in and maturity to keep in mind that this is a game in a fictional setting. When you as the player suck someones blood youre not condoning murder in the real world. I dont think we even found out the exact details of why Mark ReinHagen left but losing the literal creator of the setting and canning white wolf staff to license the game out to companies (other than onypath who do a great job) is insane. <br /> <br /> I also see they've addressed a concept called Bleed and safety in their games - what?! Anyone that has difficulties separating the game from reality needs to stay away from the game and in all seriousness speak to a mental health professional, not take the advice of a games company.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1440-lordofash","name":"LordOfAsh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1440_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T15:51:26-08:00","id":1526635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gamiem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526601#post1526601\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">vampire Mitch McConnell</div> </div> </div> </div>WHOOPS! Tautology! [/Abridged Alucard]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T16:09:07-08:00","id":1526636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526606#post1526606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">pummeling?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pummeling\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/external/images/og-image.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pummeling\" target=\"_blank\"> pummeling </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pummeling\" target=\"_blank\"> https://dictionary.cambridge.org/dictionary/english/pummeling </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> 1. an act of hitting someone or something repeatedly, especially with your&hellip; </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 12-10-2023, 07:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T16:11:51-08:00","id":1526637,"title":"","content":"The thing is that the Masquerade was kitsch. For the punk gothic scenario it was over the top, so the satyre could be delivered blow by blow. The blue bloods were so refined they could only take a specific type of blood. The shadow manipulators were so shadowy that they cast no reflection. The flesh manipulators created true nightmarish flesh constructs to do their bidding. The artists were awestruck in front of their arts. They were able to influence social structures (that weren't claimed by the rest of the WoD), fill the lore of most of the mithological vampires, fly, influence body and mind, punch through steel plates, become animals and mist. And was open enough to put the politics inside. Now is just pro forma. Frankly, I can't see the current Helena do one tenth of the old Helena. Not to say the Antes, that were supposed to be demigods and monsters of the legend. I miss the hyper dark scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-10T18:47:08-08:00","id":1526647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1525755-what-do-want-to-see-from-vtm-now?p=1526636#post1526636\" rel=