594#post1526594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. I've been buying vtm since 1992 but haven't gone near v5 for various reasons, including ludicrous modern day pandering. This is a game where players pretend to be undead blood sucking corpses FFS . Also, art work in earlier editions was awesome, photos of actors dressed up doesn't compare.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">THIS, </span>V5 kinda feels like poorly written propaganda or a certain gillete add taken up to eleven.<br /> <br /> It feels like TV publicity who centers more in selling you an agenda, than selling you the actual products. The proganda seems to be in almost every page to the point is difficult to ignore if you are in for the game. And by the way the mechanics and metaplot are also bad and inchoherent.<br /> <br /> The worst thing, is not even the people the propaganda it is directed towards is happy with it, as seen in the Chechenya incident and the anarch book.</i></span>\u200b <hr /><br /> <b><u><i><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">Do I hope things change? </span></i></u></b><i><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">NO as long as Paradox and certain writters are in charge. <u><b>This is extracted from the W5 subforum release thought thread</b></u>.<br /> <br /> <img width=\"1523\" height=\"118\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.imgur.com/2b6kjTS.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></span></i> <div align=\"right\"><i><span style=\"font-family:Georgia\">5th ed is not designed for fans</span></i></di